the model y is quickly becoming tesla's  most popular car it sold around 10 000  units in its launch year of 2020 but  that figure jumped to over 160 000 units  of model y sold in 2021. fans know that  some of the newest ev technologies like  the patented battery are coming to the  model y so let's dive into what exactly  you should expect especially if you're  not caught up with all the buzz around  this car new model y production now when  a car is launched you can expect to jump  in sales figures however a one thousand  five hundred and fifteen percent  year-on-year sales growth is a first in  the automotive market and now in quarter  two of 2022 tesla has already managed to  sell over 53 000 model wise its  popularity is why giga berlin and giga  texas tesla's two newest gigafactories  are starting out by manufacturing the  model wise exclusively the cyber rodeo  events climax in april of this year saw  the first deliveries of the new model y  according to the updated specifications  made in gigatexas strangely elon didn't  reveal any details like specs or pricing  about the new version of the electric  suv however since then i have managed to  learn a fair bit about the new car tesla  has now decided to try out their new  4680 battery cells technology first with  this car which is one of the biggest  features of the new model y but more on  that later back in berlin they are still  making and perhaps going to keep making  the model wise with the standard 2170  cells as they have been since the  introduction of the model y in 2020.  tesla and elon announced that giga  berlin hit a new milestone last week by  producing a thousand model ys in a week  this is a target they originally wanted  to hit a few months ago but they did see  a lot of supply side issues in quarter  one of 2022 which caused this delay now  if they can keep up with these  production numbers per week they'll add  50 000 model wise to tesla's yearly  capacity but the goal is to only scale  up from here and with the addition of  the new model of giga presses scheduled  to take place sometime this year or  early next year there is no reason why  they can't if you're interested to know  more about tesla's new massive giga  presses you should check out my video on  them after this one over at giga texas  is where tesla is going to make the  brand new model y utilizing the 4680  battery cell technology however we have  only seen a few confirmed deliveries so  far mainly to tesla employees who have  ordered their new model wise last year  this is very odd to see especially when  the new model has been listed as  available on tesla's website albeit in  some specific locations only now don't  get me wrong it makes perfect sense that  tesla is taking its time delivering this  new tech and wants to try it out within  the employee pool first but it is still  odd that only a handful of deliveries of  the new model y have been made since the  cyber rodeo event in april and by a  handful i mean less than 50. i would  have expected tesla to have delivered at  least 500 vehicles to have a proper go  at road testing these new model ys  before deliveries began in earnest by  2023 but we still have two more quarters  to go in this year and i am hoping  whatever problem is plaguing the  deliveries of these new models will be  solved in time anyways remember how i  said earlier on in the video that tesla  and especially elon has been very  tight-lipped about this new car well  that's true the only things i've managed  to learn about this new vehicle other  than the fact that it has the new  battery technology is its price range  and acceleration which i'm sure will be  subject to change so here it goes after  the first deliveries at the cyber rodeo  event it was leaked that the new texas  built model y standard will start at 59  990 which was at that time three  thousand dollars lower than the  long-range all-wheel drive version but  this price has gone through some  revision since then according to tesla's  website listing last month they have now  increased the base price of this new  version to 61 990 in all fairness though  due to record inflation and supply side  shortages tesla has increased prices  across board for its entire lineup the  model y long range also went from 62 990  to 65 990 and now tesla is urging some  customers who have other versions of the  model y on order especially from the  fremont plant to downgrade to this  texas-built model with the promise of  faster delivery the new model is also  going to have an epa range of 279 miles  which is 10 miles more than the normal  2022 model y version and maintains its  zero to 60 miles an hour acceleration in  five seconds although i believe tesla  will still offer its software patch  upgrade which will allow you to unlock  the acceleration boost and get it under  four seconds for about two thousand  dollars extra the new model is also  equipped with a few new features like a  magnetic center console armrest and a  parcel shelf other than these not a  whole lot is known about this new  version but not to worry i'm guessing as  people downgrade their existing orders  to this new texas-built version and  tesla starts delivering those models  over this next quarter i'll get more  information about them and you can count  on me to keep you updated on those new  features so don't forget to hit that  subscribe button and click the  notification bell so that you get to  know as soon as i release that video new  model y battery pack but let's talk  about the new battery pack more than any  other features of the new model y i am  definitely more interested in the impact  of the new 4680 battery cell and  structural battery pack and i think most  people are too it's no secret by now  that tesla is having a bit of a problem  with the manufacturing of the new  battery pack in fact elon has made this  very clear in various interviews and  tweets that they are still a few months  away from ironing out all the kinks in  this new battery technology and its mass  manufacturing process however tesla has  already announced the new model y with  this new battery technology and as i've  mentioned above already shipped a few  models out to customers unfortunately no  one has been able to confirm the exact  energy capacity of the new model y but i  heard through the grapevine that some  early texas built model y owners are now  performing some tests one of those early  owners going by spoken reviews on  youtube took the model y for a range  test and charged on a supercharger v3  and here are the results of that test  when it comes to the new energy capacity  the vehicle took a total of 59 kilowatt  hours to go from 10 state of charge to  100 now it's hard to produce a perfect  representation of the energy capacity of  these new batteries but according to  this test that would put the usable  capacity around 66 kilowatt hours in  comparison the standard 2170 battery  tesla model ys have a usable capacity of  75 kilowatt hours so what gives now we  know from inside ev's detective work  that the new 4680 battery pack has a  total of 828 cells that should put the  total usable capacity of this new  battery technology anywhere between 75  kilowatt hours to 80 kilowatt hours so  is tesla software locking these new  texas built model wise just so that  people don't cancel their older model y  orders and wait for this new one it  could very well be true that it's  intentional from tesla however i just  can't be sure until more cars are tested  out on the road as for the charging time  the new model y owner shared the details  of his charging session as well which  came out to be 9 to 50 in 12 minutes and  going up to 80 in roughly 35 minutes  which is excellent he finished the  session with a 100 charge in just over  50 minutes of course this is just one  person's test at a particular  supercharger station however i was a bit  disappointed to see that the vehicle  peaked at 227 kilowatts instead of the  250 kilowatts that the model y with the  2170 cells can achieve but i guess i  have to keep in mind that the  performance of this battery pack may  have been throttled down by tesla so  overall it appears that the 4680 battery  cell has at least a 10 higher pc rate  and average c rate with a 10 lower  usable energy capacity this makes me  super excited for the actual performance  of this new technology once the new  model y version is fully released in  2023 and tesla unlocks the potential of  this new battery pack there are also  insider rumors that tesla has allowed  some employees to test the unlocked  versions of the new model y and it meets  all the things that elon promised to us  during tesla battery day 2020 about the  new 4680 cells either way i am super  excited for tesla to finally solve its  production issues and get started with  the deliveries of the new model wise as  soon as possible but no matter if it  manages to do that in 2022 or not the  demand for these cars has never been  higher and won't go down anytime soon  according to the latest registration  data for the first five months of 2022  new tesla registrations increased by 66  year-over-year to 179  754 registrations so tesla is set up for  some insane growth in the coming years  and the new model y is definitely going  to lead that charge in the foreseeable  future so what do you think about this  new texas-built version of the model y  will tesla's new battery technology be  able to meet the lofty expectations set  by elon and if you enjoyed this video  click the one on your screen see you in  the next one

